%help
    zinc_hydro -- Apptainer/Singularity image for the Metallohydrolase enzyme
    design repository.

    This image REPLACES the lab-internal containers that older versions of the
    tutorials referred to by absolute path (crispy.sif, allmighty.sif,
    240125_shifty.sif). Those paths only ever existed inside the Baker lab
    filesystem and are gone even there. Build this instead -- it is
    self-contained and reproducible anywhere Apptainer runs.

    BUILD (needs --fakeroot or root; takes ~20-40 min and ~12 GB):

        cd Environment
        apptainer build zinc_hydro.sif zinc_hydro.def

    USE -- the runscript is the environment's python, so the image can be used
    directly wherever a python interpreter is expected:

        ./zinc_hydro.sif some_script.py --flag value
        apptainer exec --nv zinc_hydro.sif python some_script.py

    POINT THE REPO AT IT -- every script and notebook in this repository reads
    the same two environment variables, so exporting them once is enough:

        export ZINC_HYDRO_SIF=/abs/path/to/zinc_hydro.sif
        export ZINC_HYDRO_OBABEL=obabel        # optional; auto-detected

    Without ZINC_HYDRO_SIF set, everything falls back to the python interpreter
    that is currently active, which is the right answer if you installed the
    conda environment directly. You do NOT need this container.

    GPU: pass --nv to apptainer for CUDA work (RFdiffusion2/3 inference).
    The theozyme XYZ->PDB conversion and all scoring are CPU-only.

%labels
    Name        zinc_hydro
    Description Metallohydrolase enzyme design environment (RFdiffusion2/3, PyRosetta, AF2)
    Repository  https://github.com/baker-laboratory/Metallohydrolase_Enzyme_Design

Bootstrap: docker
From: condaforge/miniforge3:24.9.2-0

%files
    zinc_hydro.yml /opt/zinc_hydro.yml

%post
    set -eux

    apt-get update -y
    apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
        build-essential git wget ca-certificates aria2
    rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

    # Solve into the base prefix so no `conda activate` is needed at runtime.
    conda config --set always_yes yes --set changeps1 no
    mamba env update -n base -f /opt/zinc_hydro.yml
    mamba clean -afy

    # Trim the caches that dominate image size.
    find /opt/conda -follow -type f -name '*.a'      -delete || true
    find /opt/conda -follow -type f -name '*.pyc'    -delete || true
    rm -rf /opt/conda/pkgs

%environment
    export PATH=/opt/conda/bin:$PATH
    export PYTHONNOUSERSITE=1
    # Keep a container run from silently picking up the host's site-packages.
    export PYTHONPATH=

%runscript
    exec /opt/conda/bin/python "$@"

%test
    /opt/conda/bin/python -c "import numpy, pandas, scipy, openpyxl; print('scientific stack OK')"
    /opt/conda/bin/python -c "import pyrosetta; print('pyrosetta OK')"
    command -v obabel >/dev/null && echo "openbabel OK"
